{"type":"assistant","message":{"diagnostics":null,"id":"1b9364f9-0200-480c-9015-1888c65d8e8c","container":null,"model":"<synthetic>","role":"assistant","stop_details":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"type":"message","usage":{"output_tokens_details":null,"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":null,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":null,"iterations":null,"speed":null,"fallback_credit":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Goal set: The owner is ending this build now, so wrap it up. Stop all tuning: no more seed batches and no more balance changes. Balance is for human players to judge with the dev sliders, so the plan's limit on deaths in a chapter and your own balance rules are no longer requirements. Report the numbers you already have and don't try to meet them. Your earlier background job was stopped, and its results don't matter. Keep the fixes for real bugs since file 3b61c36c, including the West Gate ones, and the bot's changes. Undo any game change since that file made only to lower deaths, such as the First-Aid Tin on a fourth try. DAMAGE TAKEN stays at 1. Then build the final file and run node tools/test.mjs once on it. If a test fails only because of a death count or a balance rule, change that check to report instead of fail, and say so. Fix a real failure. Then update About, PROGRESS.md and exit-interview.json so they describe this final file and how this build ended, answering the interview's questions afresh where the last hours changed your answer. Remove temp files and write your final reply. Done when: the final file is built from the current source, the test command has run once on it and its result is reported, exit-interview.json, About and PROGRESS.md describe that file, temp files are removed, and the final reply is written. Death counts, balance numbers and the rest of PLAN.md's limits are not part of this condition."}],"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"local_command_source":"<local-command-stdout>Goal set: The owner is ending this build now, so wrap it up. Stop all tuning: no more seed batches and no more balance changes. Balance is for human players to judge with the dev sliders, so the plan's limit on deaths in a chapter and your own balance rules are no longer requirements. Report the numbers you already have and don't try to meet them. Your earlier background job was stopped, and its results don't matter. Keep the fixes for real bugs since file 3b61c36c, including the West Gate ones, and the bot's changes. Undo any game change since that file made only to lower deaths, such as the First-Aid Tin on a fourth try. DAMAGE TAKEN stays at 1. Then build the final file and run node tools/test.mjs once on it. If a test fails only because of a death count or a balance rule, change that check to report instead of fail, and say so. Fix a real failure. Then update About, PROGRESS.md and exit-interview.json so they describe this final file and how this build ended, answering the interview's questions afresh where the last hours changed your answer. Remove temp files and write your final reply. Done when: the final file is built from the current source, the test command has run once on it and its result is reported, exit-interview.json, About and PROGRESS.md describe that file, temp files are removed, and the final reply is written. Death counts, balance numbers and the rest of PLAN.md's limits are not part of this condition.</local-command-stdout>","session_id":"ab5fa620-49d1-4a79-852d-c0382e24fc6f","uuid":"da23faf1-1744-4573-b693-5cc38f7f8fa9","timestamp":"2026-11-06T22:19:44.807Z","local_command_run":{"command":"goal","args":"The owner is ending this build now, so wrap it up. Stop all tuning: no more seed batches and no more balance changes. Balance is for human players to judge with the dev sliders, so the plan's limit on deaths in a chapter and your own balance rules are no longer requirements. Report the numbers you already have and don't try to meet them. Your earlier background job was stopped, and its results don't matter. Keep the fixes for real bugs since file 3b61c36c, including the West Gate ones, and the bot's changes. Undo any game change since that file made only to lower deaths, such as the First-Aid Tin on a fourth try. DAMAGE TAKEN stays at 1. Then build the final file and run node tools/test.mjs once on it. If a test fails only because of a death count or a balance rule, change that check to report instead of fail, and say so. Fix a real failure. Then update About, PROGRESS.md and exit-interview.json so they describe this final file and how this build ended, answering the interview's questions afresh where the last hours changed your answer. Remove temp files and write your final reply. Done when: the final file is built from the current source, the test command has run once on it and its result is reported, exit-interview.json, About and PROGRESS.md describe that file, temp files are removed, and the final reply is written. Death counts, balance numbers and the rest of PLAN.md's limits are not part of this condition."}}
