und the soft-locks and the boss bugs. Last full measure, on 400 seeds with damage at its plain 1.0, on code that still had one extra help item since removed: every seed reached the credits, the longest stand-still was 45 s against the plan limit of 60, with 0 to 6 deaths, usually 2; 394 stayed inside the plan limit of 3 deaths a chapter and 6 reached 4; all 1200 chapter ends met my own balance rules. The final file itself has only been played by the bot on the four seeds in the test command. The owner ended the build and took the death limit and the balance rules out of the requirements: balance is for human players to judge with the dev sliders. No human has played the game.',\n  'As a target, the count of seeds over the death limit. Reading the runs behind it found real bugs, but once those ran out the count moved between 2 and 6 of 400 by chance, and I spent hours chasing it. Of the checks that ran every time, the one for a browser without WebGPU: it passed the first time and never failed again.',\n\"\"\"\ns=s[:i]+new+s[j:]\nold=\"I found it very late and wrapped its query to ignore them.'\"\nassert old in s\ns=s.replace(old,\"I found it very late and wrapped its query to ignore them. A headless run also only repeats at the same step size: stepping 6 frames at a time and 30 at a time played different games on one seed, and I did not find out why.'\")\ni=s.index('export const PROMPT_FEEDBACK = [')\nj=s.index('];',i)\nnew = \"\"\"export const PROMPT_FEEDBACK = [\n  'The plan was specific and had a voice: a whole world, a script, real numbers and a tone to hit. And the section on this computer said exactly what to use in place of a pad, a phone and a second player.',\n  'TASK.md still asks me to pick the genre and perspective, while PLAN.md had already decided them. I followed the plan. The plan also sets a limit of 3 deaths a chapter for a bot, which measures the bot as much as the game, and it does not say whether that means one run or every run. The completion check read it as every run, which no finite test can show, and I kept tuning against it when I should have said so sooner. The owner settled it by ending the build.',\n  'Balance without a human. Every system worked long before the game was fair, and a bot only tells you what kills a bot. I can show the game can be finished. I can not say how it feels to play. The other hard thing was knowing when to stop: the same measure that found the worst bugs went on asking for more after they were gone.',\n  'Name what to cut first if a run gets long, give balance targets for a kind of player, not only for a script, and say when a balance number is something to report and when it is a condition for being done.',\n\"\"\"\ns=s[:i]+new+s[j:]\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\np='docs/PLAN-CHECK.md'; s=open(p).read()\nold=\"- **Where the plan's map or props needed help.** A body-only wall round every map, because the causeway's floor reaches the edge of its grid;\"\nnew_=\"- **How balance ended.** The owner ended the build and took the plan's death limit and these balance rules out of the requirements: balance is for human players to judge with the dev sliders. Numbers from the last full measure are in `../PROGRESS.md`.\\n- **Where the plan's map or props needed help.** The West Gate's exit is the gate's own cells, not the floor in front of it. A body-only wall round every map, because the causeway's floor reaches the edge of its grid;\"\nassert old in s; s=s.replace(old,new_)\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nEOF\nnode -e \"import('./src/data/about.js').then(m=>{console.log(m.TESTING_FEEDBACK.length,m.ENGINE_FEEDBACK.length,m.PROMPT_FEEDBACK.length)})\"; grep -nP \"[^\\x00-\\x7F]\" src/data/about.js | cut -c1-80 | head -3; node tools/build.mjs 2>&1 | tail -1 | cut -c1-120; H=$(ls ../RegrettableEvil4-*.html); echo \"final file $(sha256sum $H | cut -c1-24)\"; mkdir -p .scratch; (node tools/test.mjs > .scratch/final-test.log 2>&1; echo \"exit $?\" >> .scratch/final-test.log; echo \"after $(sha256sum $H | c